H-48 bandit real-reward frozen test fixture.

arm G: high execution-grounded reward (worst_case = 0.85 from H-45 aggregate).
arm B: low execution-grounded reward (worst_case = 0.10 from H-45 aggregate).

The fixture is used by h48_bandit_real_reward_contract.rs to verify:
  - bandit converges to arm G over sufficient updates (real reward, not bytes)
  - broken arm (--bandit-reward-from-bytes) converges to arm B (R2 falsifiability)
  - Successive-Rejects SR identifies arm G as best-arm under a fixed budget
  - ExIt curriculum seed from partial history propagates to posteriors

Convergence criterion: after N_CONVERGENCE_ROUNDS updates, select_next_arm
returns arm G index in at least CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD fraction of draws.

Gate-frozen (R8): this directory is read-only to the running generation loop.
No candidate can inject into or modify this fixture.

Discount factor for the fixture: FIXTURE_GAMMA = 0.90 (per arXiv:2305.10718
S5 experiments: less aggressive forgetting on short horizons; the production
DEFAULT_DISCOUNT_FACTOR = 0.0357 is for multi-generation live loops and
causes over-forgetting on the compact fixture run).
